;;; An activator a rule derives binds a relation parameter to a fact, and the
;;; run stopped where its plan is compiled; the witness of a regression row
;;; that is gone, since the static check flags the program and no row holds
;;; a flagged program's answer (Q-M1f.564).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A rule `r` whose parameter `?R` names a relation, `(box (?R b))`, and a
;;; rule `mk` that derives `r`'s activator from `item`'s argument, `(r ?f)`.
;;; `item` is a declared relation, so its argument holds any object, a fact
;;; among them, and `(item (a b))` is one: `mk` derives `(r (a b))`, which
;;; binds `?R` to the fact `(a b)`.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The program loaded, root fired `mk` and derived `(r (a b))`, and the run
;;; stopped where `r`'s plan is compiled, exit 1, with the compiler's line, *the relation
;;; head ?R of (?R b) at Loc(…) is bound to the fact (a b) — a relation is
;;; named by a symbol, not a fact.*, on every command (`ein solve FILE` at
;;; `8249e872`, release and debug alike). The loader then refused it, exit
;;; 1. Without `(item (a b))` it answered: `derived-activator-never.ein`.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Every command loads the program, exit 0. Root derives `(r (a b))`,
;;; holds it as the fact it is, and compiles no plan of `r` for it: the
;;; activator activates nothing, and no command says so, at the load or at
;;; a run, as none says so of an activator of another count (Q-M1f.1). No
;;; run stops. The static check flags the program, so nothing is claimed of
;;; its answer.
;;;

(relation box Node :why "{?3} is in the box")
(relation hit Node :why "{?3} is hit")
(relation item Node :why "{?3} is an item")
(box (a b))
(rule r (?R)
  :match (box (?R b))
  :assert (hit z)
  :why "a box holds a {?R} of b")
(rule mk ()
  :match (item ?f)
  :assert (r ?f)
  :why "{?f} is an item, so r is asked of it")
(item (a b))
(query :goal (hit ?x))
